{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_sharding_overview_clustersharding", "label": "ClusterSharding", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "One actor per entity key spread across nodes with automatic rebalancing; cluster.sharding is a memoised facade so repeated reads return the same instance. Starting the same type twice on one node throws, because the second call used to return the first's region and a hosting node could silently get a proxy whose placeholder factory throws when a shard lands.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/sharding/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_sharding_overview_region", "label": "Shard region actor", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "One per node: routes messages to the right shard's owner and decides when local entities - and shards left empty - passivate, because only it sees traffic across every shard on this node, which is why maxEntities is a per-node cap.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/sharding/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_sharding_overview_shard", "label": "Shard actor", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "A child of the region owning the entity actors; it goes away once it has stood empty for its window and comes back with the next message, which is what makes a shard addressable at all.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/sharding/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_sharding_overview_shardcoordinator", "label": "Shard coordinator", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "One per cluster, a singleton on the leader; decides which node owns each shard and handles rebalancing on membership changes and on a region shutting down.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/sharding/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_sharding_overview_entity", "label": "Sharded entity actor", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "One per entityId, a child of its shard on whichever node owns the shard the id hashes to; identical restart semantics to any actor, so state that must survive a move needs PersistentActor, DurableStateActor or DistributedData.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/sharding/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_sharding_overview_shardkey", "label": "ShardKey", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Identity is the typeName alone; the extractor rides along so the declaring class is the single source of truth, and a lookup-only node can name the same type without one. The explicit type argument is load-bearing - without it every ref degrades to ActorRef<unknown>.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/sharding/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_sharding_overview_entityid", "label": "this.entityId", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "The value extractEntityId returned, unchanged; the context is attached after the constructor, so a persistenceId must be a getter rather than a field. The identity is set on the entity and nowhere else, so an entity's own children get None.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/sharding/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_sharding_overview_numshards_agreement", "label": "numShards is a cluster-wide agreement", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Every node computes hash(entityId) % numShards itself, so two nodes with different counts run the same entity in two non-colliding paths - two writers on one persistenceId. The count travels in the region's registration and the coordinator refuses a disagreeing region, which stalls with an error rather than splitting silently; proxies count too, and the verdict is a log line because registration is asynchronous with no call to throw from.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/sharding/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_sharding_overview_passivation", "label": "Entity passivation", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Stops an idle entity after passivationIdleMs (default five minutes) or when maxEntities evicts the LRU; the region buffers messages arriving while it stops and replays them to the fresh incarnation. In-memory state does not survive it - a PersistentActor replays and notices nothing, a plain actor starts over.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/sharding/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_sharding_overview_shard_passivation", "label": "Shards passivate too", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Passivating every entity used to leave a live actor holding an empty map, and since ids spread over the hash space a long-running node eventually kept all 64. The region keeps ownership so only the actor goes: the shard stays routable and the next message re-creates shard and entity together with no coordinator round trip.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/sharding/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_sharding_overview_passivate", "label": "Passivate message", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Carries a stop-message forwarded back to the entity, so the entity decides when and how it shuts down - finish in-flight work, flush state, then terminate.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/sharding/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_sharding_overview_shardingoptions", "label": "ShardingOptionsType / StartShardingOptions", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Five fields are also HOCON keys that set the node-wide baseline and sit under whatever start(...) passes explicitly, so a per-type builder value still wins; sharing number-of-shards in one config file is the least error-prone way to keep nodes in step.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/sharding/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_sharding_overview_entity_name_escaping", "label": "Injective entity-name escaping", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Actor names have a restricted alphabet, so the shard escapes anything a name cannot carry; the escape is injective because a shared name would make the second entity spawn under a taken name and the throw would kill the shard and every entity in it. Nothing decodes a path segment - the path is a label, entityId is the value.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/sharding/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_sharding_overview_clustersharding", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_sharding_overview_region", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/sharding/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "